@startuml Feature_UseCase

actor User
participant "Serial-I2C\nBridge Board" as Bridge
participant "I2C Target\nDevice" as Target

== I2C Configuration Use Case ==
User -> Bridge: Send serial request:\nConfigure I2C (address, speed)
Bridge -> Bridge: Save configuration\nto non-volatile storage
Bridge --> User: Serial response:\nConfiguration successful

== I2C Write Use Case ==
User -> Bridge: Send serial request:\nWrite data to I2C device (addr, reg, data)
Bridge -> Target: I2C write transfer\n(START + addr + reg + data + STOP)
Target --> Bridge: ACK
Bridge --> User: Serial response:\nWrite successful

== I2C Read Use Case ==
User -> Bridge: Send serial request:\nRead data from I2C device (addr, reg, length)
Bridge -> Target: I2C read transfer\n(START + addr + reg + RESTART + read + STOP)
Target --> Bridge: I2C data bytes
Bridge --> User: Serial response:\nRead data bytes

note right of User
  User communicates with I2C
  peripherals (sensors, EEPROMs,
  displays) via simple serial commands
end note

@enduml
